A package source stopped publishing: its newest index is older
than Tigris_Repos_MaxAge days (90 by default) and no suite of it
re-fetched since, so the packages installed from it sit unpatched
while the manager says the system is up to date. Each repository
is judged by its newest suite: a release pocket never changes by
design, its updates do. dnf and zypper repositories are judged with
the others from the same host, so Fedora's fedora and openSUSE's
repo-oss, frozen at release, count as alive while their updates
repositories are; a host serving many publishers (OBS, COPR) is
split by project. Local repositories (file:, cd: and the like) and
openh264 codec repositories are not judged. Drop the source, move
to its successor, or track its -updates suite too.
